  "body": "## Goal\nMap zero-context git diff hunks to canonical Rust function keys in `xtask`.\n\n## Scope\n- Add `syn` (already in `Cargo.lock` at `2.0.119`, with `full` and `visit` features) to `xtask/Cargo.toml`.\n- Add `xtask/src/diff_fns.rs` to parse old and new `.rs` files from `git show <base>:<path>` and the working tree.\n- Walk each file AST and emit canonical keys in the form `<crate>::<module>::[<Type>::]<fn>`.\n- Fold closures and nested helper functions into the enclosing function key.\n- Detect file renames with `git diff -M` so moved files match old function keys.\n- Mark hunks outside any function (constants, structs, enums, macros, imports) as file-level hits.\n- Emit deleted function keys from the old file AST.\n\n## Done means\n`cargo test -p xtask` passes unit tests for edited, added, deleted, renamed, method, closure, and top-level hunks, and a fixture test maps the diff of PR #2664 to `camcraft_app::geometry::import::step::shell_facets` and `camcraft_app::geometry::import::step_facets::facets_of`.\n\nPart of #2738",
